{
    /* A softmax, and the count of the entries it puts above a tenth.

       The board operations are glyphs because they describe a shape. These are
       named because they describe a quantity — which is the same line Wasan
       drew: enri (円理), Seki and Takebe's theory of series, was how the
       analytic functions were reached, and it was a named technique rather
       than a movement of beads. */
    INPUT:◯ □ 1024 1

    exp INPUT → E
    (E / (□0 (◇+ E))) → P

    /* ind turns a test into 1 or 0, which is what lets a fold count.
       A mask cannot: one that passes a value which happens to be zero is
       indistinguishable from one that blocked it. */
    (ind (P > 0.001)) → ABOVE

    (□0 (◇+ ABOVE)) → OUTPUT
    ! (OUTPUT >= 0.0)

    OUTPUT → =
}
